      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "In nineteen sixty, the United States produced roughly forty percent of all global output. It was the undisputed giant.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "globe",
          "big": "~40%",
          "label": "US share of world output, 1960",
          "props": [
            "chartUp",
            "globe"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Gross domestic product is the total value of what an economy produces.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-gdp",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · GDP"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Today that share is closer to a quarter, even though America itself kept growing the whole time.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "thennow",
          "kicker": "US share of world GDP",
          "thenLabel": "1960",
          "thenValue": "~40%",
          "nowLabel": "Today",
          "nowValue": "~25%",
          "sub": "America grew — the world grew faster"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The key point is that this isn't America shrinking. It's the rest of the world catching up.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "globe",
          "kicker": "what really happened",
          "line": "Others caught up",
          "sub": "not a US collapse"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Economists call it convergence, poorer economies tending to grow faster.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-conv",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · convergence"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "As China, India and others industrialized, the global pie got far bigger, and more evenly split.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "globe",
          "big": "bigger pie",
          "label": "more evenly shared",
